From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Umair Ahmed Shah <umairahmedshah@hotmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 18:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] rzv2l: export the boot ROM device in /chosen

The boot ROM loads BL2 from the device selected by the board's mode
switches and latches the choice in SYS_LSI_MODE. Nothing after BL2
reports it, and Linux cannot infer it: a QSPI bootchain can boot a
kernel and rootfs from SD or eMMC.

Read the latched mode when bootm finalises the kernel device tree and
store it as /chosen/edge,boot-source ("qspi", "esd", "emmc", "scif" or
"unknown"), with an [EDGE] console marker for serial logs.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board-specific boot-source reporting]
Assisted-by: claude-code:claude-opus-5-5
---
 board/renesas/rzv2l-dev/rzv2l-dev.c | 28 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 28 insertions(+)

--- a/board/renesas/rzv2l-dev/rzv2l-dev.c
+++ b/board/renesas/rzv2l-dev/rzv2l-dev.c
@@ -271,11 +271,39 @@
 	"/soc/mmc@11c00000", "vqmmc-supply", "<&/regulator-vccq-sdhi0>",
 };
 
+static const char *edge_boot_source(u32 md_boot)
+{
+	switch (md_boot) {
+	case 0:
+		return "esd";
+	case 1:
+	case 2:
+		return "emmc";
+	case 3:
+	case 4:
+		return "qspi";
+	case 5:
+		return "scif";
+	default:
+		return "unknown";
+	}
+}
+
 int ft_verify_fdt(void *fdt)
 {
 	const char **fdt_dt = NULL;
 	int size = 0;
 	u32 boot_mode = readl(SYS_LSI_MODE);
+	const char *src = edge_boot_source(boot_mode &
+					   SYS_LSI_MODE_STAT_MD_BOOT_MASK);
+	int chosen = fdt_path_offset(fdt, "/chosen");
+
+	/* Boot ROM device for userspace: /proc/device-tree/chosen/edge,boot-source */
+	if (chosen < 0 ||
+	    fdt_setprop_string(fdt, chosen, "edge,boot-source", src))
+		printf("[EDGE] UBOOT boot-source=%s FAILED fdt\n", src);
+	else
+		printf("[EDGE] UBOOT boot-source=%s\n", src);
 
 	switch (boot_mode & SYS_LSI_MODE_STAT_MD_BOOT_MASK) {
 	case ESD_MODE:
